  {p:"P1", region:"Japan", headline:"Bank of Japan launches a DLT sandbox to study central bank money in tokenised form; a senior official says stablecoin reserves need regulation",
   lede:"Bank of Japan Executive Director Kamiyama Kazushige told an IMF seminar in Tokyo on 27 November that the BOJ has launched a DLT Sandbox Project to examine the implications of DLT and tokenisation for money and market infrastructure, including providing central bank money in tokenised form. He said forms of money such as stablecoins need appropriate regulation of reserves and arrangements, together with well-designed links to central bank money, to preserve the singleness of money.",
   points:["The sandbox is being built with holders of current accounts at the BOJ; use cases focus on cross-border payments, domestic interbank settlement, and funds settlement of tokenised Japanese government bonds","The BOJ says tokenising central bank money is one option and linking existing infrastructure to new platforms is another, to be chosen on market needs","The BOJ also takes part in the BIS Project Agorá, which brings tokenised commercial bank deposits and tokenised central bank money onto a shared platform for cross-border payments","The speech noted the government's push for on-chain finance, with the FSA leading a public-private roadmap; retail CBDC work continues in a pilot, with no decision to issue"],
   bank:["Track how Taiwan's central bank positions its tokenised payment platform, issuing tokenised central bank money or linking existing systems to new platforms, as this will shape interbank settlement for deposit tokens","When commenting to the FSC and the central bank, cite the BOJ's call for reserve regulation plus links to central bank money in support of the reserve-deposit design","Banks with Japanese business should follow the three megabanks' participation in Project Agorá"],
   view:"The BOJ is moving in the same direction as Singapore and Hong Kong: settle the role of central bank money in a tokenised setting first, then connect deposit tokens and stablecoins. Taiwan's central bank, with its new stablecoin reserve rule, is starting from the same link to central bank money.",
   links:[["BOJ speech (PDF)","https://www.boj.or.jp/en/about/press/koen_2026/data/ko261127a.pdf",false],["The Block","https://www.theblock.co/news/regulation/2026-11-27-bank-of-japan-official-says-stablecoins-need-reserve-rules-to-preserve-singleness-of-money-447059",true]]}
